    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0593" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 337.11/452</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Gonzales
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-19T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 19, 1917, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Bethlehem Steel Company advise Department of report from its manager that
                    anti-American feeling very strong among rebels, that the mines are practically
                    without adequate protection as marines are kept constantly moving and that Cuban
                    Government cannot end trouble without substantial assistance.</p>
                <p>You will communicate this information to President Menocal and ascertain why
                    ample and permanent protection is not furnished these properties. Report by
                    cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
